{"id":"inkhorn","name":"Inkhorn","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:inkhorn"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Inkhorn","text":"The Hebrew word so rendered means simply a round vessel or cup for containing ink, which was generally worn by writers in the girdle (Ezek. 9:2, 3, 11). The word “inkhorn” was used by the translators, because in former times in this country horns were used for containing ink."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H7083","lemma":"קֶסֶת","xlit":"qeçeth","gloss":"a cup","kjv":"inkhorn","count":3,"share":1},{"strong":"H906","lemma":"בַּד","xlit":"bad","gloss":"flaxen thread or yarn","kjv":"linen","count":3,"share":1},{"strong":"H4975","lemma":"מֹתֶן","xlit":"môthen","gloss":"the waist or small of the back","kjv":"greyhound, loins, side","count":3,"share":1},{"strong":"H3847","lemma":"לָבַשׁ","xlit":"lâbash","gloss":"wrap around","kjv":"apparel, arm, array, clothe","count":3,"share":1},{"strong":"H5608","lemma":"סָפַר","xlit":"çâphar","gloss":"to score with a mark as a tally or record","kjv":"commune, count; declare, number, penknife","count":2,"share":0.67}],"verses":["Ezek.9.2","Ezek.9.3","Ezek.9.11"],"related":[{"id":"breeches","type":"lexical","strong":"H906","why":"both lead with בַּד (H906)"}],"works":[]}
